@Serializable
data class PlaybackSnapshot(
    val phase: PlaybackPhase,
    /** Loopback URL for the player, once `ready`. */
    val url: String? = null,
    /** The version that is playing: the picked key or one of its failovers. */
    val key: String? = null,
    /** The source the view adopted last: one more each time it moves to a new source, never reused in the view's life (0 before the first). Two sources of one `key` (two installs listing the same link) differ here; `failOver` names it. */
    val attempt: Long,
    /** `url` is a manifest the core rewrote, not a file: HLS (its name ends in `.m3u8`) or DASH (`.mpd`). */
    val manifest: Boolean,
    val filename: String? = null,
    val sizeBytes: Long? = null,
    /** Where to start, from saved progress. */
    val resumeMs: Long? = null,
    /** Sources that failed, in order, each with a plain reason. */
    val attempts: List<Attempt> = emptyList(),
    /** External subtitles: the stream's own, then each subtitles addon's, as they arrive. */
    val subtitles: List<SubtitleTrack> = emptyList(),
    /** Subtitles addons are still being asked. */
    val subtitlesPending: Boolean,
    /** Subtitle sources that gave nothing this time, each once, shown under the subtitle list (plans/m13-turkcealtyazi.md 4.2). */
    val subtitleNotes: List<SubtitleNote> = emptyList(),
    /** The track (its `url`) every app turns on at start, once, when the list has settled: the profile set subtitle languages and the audio is in none of them, or the user chose one for this title before. Null otherwise. The user's own pick, or Off, always wins: send `subtitleChosen` (plans/m13-subtitle-languages.md 6). */
    val autoSubtitle: String? = null,
    /** The track (its `url`) the apps show as the second subtitle line (plans/dual-subtitles.md 3.2), until the viewer picks one in this play (`secondSubtitleChosen`): the profile's `secondSubtitle` language, the spoken one for `"audio"`, never the first line's language. A level, not a one-time start: it changes, or goes null, when the first line changes. Draw it only while a first line is on. */
    val autoSecondSubtitle: String? = null,
    /** The tag the core reads the audio in (the probe's default audio track, else the release name's first language), set with the start subtitle; null when not known: the picker's "Spoken language" row names it. */
    val spokenLanguage: String? = null,
    /** Every track the start subtitle could turn on failed to read: each one that failed handed over to the next best (its language's next, then the next language, as `autoSubtitle` changes) and none was left. A neutral state with no source: the apps show `player.subtitlesFailed` from apps/shared/stream-choice-words.json. */
    val startSubtitleFailed: Boolean = false,
    /** The playing file has an audio track described for blind and low-vision viewers (its container flag or its name, read as the file opens): the player's AD mark (core backlog C35). */
    val audioDescription: Boolean = false,
    /** The audio languages every app starts the file in, most wanted first: the profile's audio languages when the user chose some, else the title's original language once TMDB names it. A player turns on the first of them the file has; with none of them in the file, or an empty list, its own pick (the device's language) stands. */
    val audioLanguages: List<String> = emptyList(),
    /** The next released episode, for an Up Next card. */
    val next: NextEpisode? = null,
    /** The playing stream's binge group; pass it as `bingeGroup` when opening Versions for the next episode so the same release line is picked. */
    val bingeGroup: String? = null,
    /** Skip segments of the playing version, once its duration is reported. */
    val segments: List<Segment> = emptyList(),
    /** When to offer the Up Next card: the credits start from a source that matched the release; null keeps the app's own timing. */
    val nextAtMs: Long? = null,
    /** Trakt's side: `on` scrobbles, `unmapped` (Trakt cannot name it), `off`, `thisDeviceOff` (the profile uses Trakt, this device is not signed in). */
    val trakt: TraktPlayback,
    /** The recommended version failed for a reason of its own (no picture on this device, a dead swarm, the wrong file) and the view moved on by itself to this one, the ranking's next pick, at most twice: "Trying the next version: {label}" while `phase` is `resolving`. Cleared once a source of it starts. */
    val trying: OtherVersion? = null,
    /** A version picked by hand failed for a reason of its own: the failure card offers this one, the ranking's next pick (open `playback` with its key from the same Versions subscription). */
    val offer: OtherVersion? = null,
    /** "Try again" taken in this view: one more each time it is accepted, so a retry that fails again at once still differs from the failure before it (code review 2026-10-20 r2 P3-6). Show "Trying again". */
    val retries: Int = 0,
    /** How far the start is while `phase` is `resolving`: the loading screen's fill and its words (plans/player-polish.md 1.3). Null before the first source starts and from `ready` on. */
    val start: StartProgress? = null,
    /** The version playing is not the one the start announced: the recommendation moved on (`trying`) and this one plays. The core's words, for the apps to show once from `ready`: "Playing 720p WEB: the 1080p Blu-ray did not start here", "... did not play on this device". Null otherwise. */
    val moved: String? = null,
    /** The start has taken `CHOOSE_AFTER` (20 s): the loading screen shows the quiet "Choose another version" beside Back (plans/play-every-version.md 2e). */
    val chooseAnother: Boolean = false,
    /** Why nothing played, once `phase` is `failed`: the zero-playable words for what happened (`empty.<kind>` in stream-choice-words.json): notStarted when the start's budget ran out; else nothingPlaysHere when every failure was the versions' own on this device, else unreachable. */
    val empty: EmptyKind? = null,
    /** When a first play's start budget (90 s from its first attempt's add) ends, in epoch ms, while it runs: from the first attempt until a source played past its start (or the playback failed). Time the app spends after `ready` (another player engine opening the file) counts against it too (plans/apple-second-engine.md 2.3). Null otherwise. An app reads it only while it is still opening the source: a video that plays, or is paused, before its first 30 s is never failed by it. */
    val startBudgetEndsAt: Long? = null,
    /** The container of the file playing ("mkv", "mp4"), once `ready`: the opened file's name as the core parses it, else what an earlier play of this version opened, else the release's; null when unknown. Apple picks its player engine by it (plans/apple-second-engine.md 2.1). */
    val container: String? = null,
    /** The playing release's audio formats in the core's names ("dts_hd_ma", "true_hd", "atmos"), once `ready`; empty when unknown. */
    val audio: List<String> = emptyList(),
    /** The second engine this version played on here before (`playedOn`), after the first refused it ("aether"): the app opens it there first. */
    val engine: String? = null,
)

